## Modified API Interface

The sudopod `DeployOptions` interface needs a top-level `dev` boolean:

```typescript
export interface DeployOptions {
  /** Git repository configuration */
  git: {
    owner: string;
    repo: string;
    branch?: string;
  };

  /** Development mode - install sudocode from local build instead of npm */
  dev?: boolean;  // NEW: Top-level boolean

  /** Override workspace directory (optional) */
  workspaceDir?: string;

  /** Agent configuration */
  agents?: {
    install: string[];
  };

  /** Model/LLM configuration */
  models?: {
    claudeLtt?: string;
    providerConfig?: Record<string, any>;
    providerConfigEnvVar?: string;
  };

  /** Sudocode installation configuration */
  sudocode: {
    /** Installation mode: npm or local build */
    mode: 'npm' | 'local';  // KEEP: This determines HOW to install (npm version vs local path)

    /** Specific version for npm mode */
    version?: string;

    /** Path to local build for local mode */
    localPath?: string;
  };

  /** Server configuration */
  server: {
    port?: number;
    keepAliveHours?: number;
    idleTimeout?: number;
  };

  /** Provider-specific options */
  providerOptions: CodespacesDeployOptions | CoderDeployOptions;
}
```

**Clarification:**
- `dev` at top level: Boolean flag indicating "use local repository for installation"
- `sudocode.mode`: Specifies the installation mechanism (npm vs local build)
- When `dev: true`, typically `sudocode.mode` would be `'local'`
- The `dev` flag can also influence other behavior (branch selection, testing, etc.)

